**Assignment Title** Studio 3.3 
**Prompt** The Art Revolution and Redefinition Manifesto
Assignment Title: Promotional Landing Page
Prompt: Create an image for a promotional landing page for a contemporary global biennial exhibition titled “Tradition & Transformation: Same Humanity, New Stories.” The historic tradition is Greek Idealism, paired with the modern social value of identity and self-expression. The main image will be classical white marble Greek statue beside a confident contemporary woman make her face and clothing bold, colorful pop art shapes to help express her confidence. Add greek columns and a modern city skyline behind them to show the past and present in the same space. Use Pop Art as the main contemporary art style, the colors used should be vivid hot pink, green, electric blue, yellow, black, and marble white. Use clear contour lines around the statue and portrait, and sweeping directional lines that go diagonally and horizontally across the page to help the viewers eyes go across the page. Use intense value contrast between the white marble and deep black areas, and some color contrast between blue and green, to make the contemporary portrait the focal point. The design should feel energetic, inclusive, and professional. showing that an idealized ancient body can be reinterpreted through contemporary voices rather than treated as the only standard of beauty. Use legible editorial typography and a strong visual hierarchy. Also arrange the page like a exhibition website with a top navigation bar, a large title, a short exhibition description, fictional dates and a footer with visit and ticket links.
Vocabulary: Vocabulary Breakdown

Contemporary Art

To me, contemporary art is art made in and around our own time that responds to the world people are living in. Using traditional materials or newer forms.

Pop Art

Pop Art borrows the bold colors, strong outlines, and attention-grabbing look of advertising, comics, celebrities, and everyday popular culture.
Directional Lines

Directional lines are marks or edges that help lead the viewer’s eye through a composition. 

Value Contrast

Value contrast is the difference between light and dark areas. Like the bright marble and vivid portrait stand out against dark sections, so the main images are easy to notice.

Focal Point

The focal point is the part of the design that attracts attention first. Here, the classical statue beside the colorful contemporary woman is meant to be the first thing viewers notice because it expresses the meeting of tradition and self-expression.
